        "text": "DRY",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "definition_text": {
        "text": "In programming we have this concept called DRY which is short for don't repeat yourself; repeating expressions is not a good solution.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "context": null
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "example_type": null,
      "example_text": {
        "text": "If the number is divisible by 5 and 3, print fizzbuzz; otherwise if divisible by 5, print fizz; else if divisible by 3, print buzz; else print the number.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "exemplifies": {
        "text": "FizzBuzz problem solution with specific conditions first",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      }
    },
    {
      "example_type": null,
      "example_text": {
        "text": "First check if the number is divisible by 5; if also divisible by 3, print fizzbuzz, else print fizz. Then check if divisible by 3 and print buzz; otherwise print the number.",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "exemplifies": {
        "text": "Alternative FizzBuzz solution using nested if-else to avoid repetition",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      }
    },
    {
      "example_type": null,
      "example_text": {
        "text": "Printing a hello world message five times without repeating the print statement.",
        "refs": ["Q0005"]
      },
      "exemplifies": {
        "text": "Demonstration of repetition for repeated actions",
        "refs": ["Q0005"]
      }
    }
  ],
  "explanations": [
    {
      "topic": {
        "text": "Ordering of conditions in if-else chains",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null,
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "Place the most specific conditions at the top and the most generic ones at the bottom to ensure correct execution.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": {
        "text": "Trade-offs in code structure",
        "refs": ["Q0003", "Q0004"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null,
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "Nested if-else statements can make code harder to read, while a flat structure may involve some repetition but is cleaner and easier to understand.",
        "refs": ["Q0003", "Q0004"]
      }
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "fact_type": null,
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Nested if-else statements are considered bad practice because they increase code complexity and reduce readability.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      }
    },
    {
      "fact_type": null,
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "A flat if-else structure without nesting is cleaner and easier to read, even if it includes some repetition.",
